284	\begin{remark}[The extension to general $k$ is not coordinatewise]\label{rem:ld-soundness-simultaneity}
285		The extension from $k = 1$ to general $k$ cited in the proof of Theorem~\ref{lem:ld-soundness} is the reduction deriving Theorem~4.43 from Theorem~4.40 in \cite{Natarajan2018NEEXP}: the $k$ answer polynomials are combined into the single polynomial $(\alpha, u) \mapsto \sum_i \alpha_i g_i(u)$ in $m + k$ variables, whose restriction to a queried subspace has degree $d + 1$; the case $k = 1$ is applied once to the combined strategy at that degree, and the $k$ polynomials are recovered from the resulting measurement by exact linearity in $\alpha$ and the Schwartz--Zippel lemma at degree $d + 1$. It cannot be replaced by applying the case $k = 1$ to each coordinate separately and combining the coordinate measurements by the sandwich of Lemma~\ref{lem:ld-sandwich}: over $\F_{2^s}$ with $d = 1$ and $k = 2$ there are a joint point measurement and coordinate polynomial measurements, on the maximally entangled state, for which every coordinate relation of the theorem holds with error $0$ while every POVM with polynomial-pair outcomes has consistency defect at least $1 - 2/q$ against the joint point measurement; the computation is in \cite{gap:qpbt_ld-simultaneous-sandwich}. The formalization accordingly proves, for $k = 1$, the polynomial-tuple conclusion of Theorem~\ref{lem:ld-soundness} with its three consistency defects bounded by the error function of Theorem~\ref{thm:main-formal} at the auxiliary sampling parameter $2560000\,m^3d$ and pass bound $3\eps$, and not by $\delta_{\mathrm{ld}}$: the absorption of that error into $\delta_{\mathrm{ld}}$ is a separate estimate, and the identification of the two games remains open. The value $k = 1$ is the only one instantiated in the proof of Lemma~\ref{lem:qld-4-7}; the general case awaits a formalization of the combining reduction. That case is Theorem~\ref{lem:ld-soundness-k-one} below. The one-coordinate conclusion, obtained for the directly indexed game of Remark~\ref{rem:qld-4-7-divisibility}, is Lemma~\ref{lem:direct-